    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d529">

                <pb facs="0695" n="683" xml:id="pg683"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/8–1546: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Prime Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Attlee</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to President Truman </hi><anchor
                        n="44" xml:id="d529-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-08-15">15 August 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Personal and Top Secret. Thank you for your personal message of August 13th [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">12th</hi>]. I have now received from the Foreign
                    Secretary in Paris a copy of the message sent by the State Department to Mr.
                    Byrnes and Mr. Harriman. We are discussing these proposals and it will probably
                    take a few days before we can give our views on them.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d529-f1" n="44" type="source" xml:id="d529-f1-content">
                <p>Copy transmitted to Mr. Acheson by the British Minister in Washington (Balfour)
                    on August 15.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
